ase compliance, and kicks off the mediation process and resolves 98% of South Carolina cases before they ever reach a courtroom</p></div><div class="MuiStack-root mui-1o9tb1h"><div class="MuiStack-root mui-swf3lo"><div class="MuiStack-root mui-qfnw5i"><div class="MuiBox-root mui-vbfzuw"><p class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-33x7jd">Local ordinance</p></div><p class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-1oh5523">Myrtle Beach Rent Ordinance</p></div><p class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-1pbz32v">Myrtle Beach has no rent-control ordinance. South Carolina state law preempts local rent control, so cities and towns cannot cap rent increases. Landlords may raise rent by any amount at the end of a lease term with proper notice, subject to federal fair-housing and anti-retaliation protections.</p></div><div class="MuiStack-root mui-swf3lo"><div class="MuiStack-root mui-qfnw5i"><div class="MuiBox-root mui-vbfzuw"><p class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-33x7jd">Fun fact</p></div><p class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-1oh5523">Fun Facts about Myrtle Beach</p></div><p class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-1pbz32v">Did you know South Carolina bans local rent control? No city in the state, including Myrtle Beach, can set its own cap.</p></div></div></div><div class="MuiBox-root mui-1th3fel"><div class="MuiBox-root mui-ijnhfw" id="testimonials-slider-section"><div class="MuiStack-root mui-nwltbd"><div class="MuiStack-root mui-90qip8"><h2 class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h2 mui-kbdtl">Long-term rentals, under control.</h2><p class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-1m3340g">Whether youâ€™re an owner, property manager, real estate agent, or brokerage, Hemlane provides a professional and stress-free way to manage your rentals, use AI and real human support.</p></div><div class="MuiBox-root mui-1dgmx46"><div style="position:relative;width:100%;top:0;left:0;opacity:1;transform:none"><div class="Mu