+			<td colspan="4" style><span class="inlinep"><span class="bold"><strong>Note:</strong></span> Be sure to use only the personal portion of your casualty losses (and gains) when completing Section A of the separate Form 4684 you attach to your return. The separate Form 4684 you attach to your return is used to figure the casualty losses you can include on line 15 of Schedule A and the net qualified disaster losses you can include on line 16 of Schedule A. You will report casualty and theft losses attributable to your rental activity in Section B of the separate Form 4684 you attach to your return.</span></td>
