+			<td style><span class="inlinep">&nbsp;</span></td>
+		</tr>
+		<tr>
+			<td style><span class="inlinep"><span class="bold"><strong>Line 6e.</strong></span> </span></td>
+			<td colspan="4" style><span class="inlinep">You can deduct the amounts on lines 6a, 6b, and 6c as rental expenses only to the extent they arenâ€™t more than the amount on line 6e.* Include the depreciation from line 6e, if any, on the appropriate line of Schedule E. Include the casualty loss from line 6e, if any, with the casualty loss from line 2c in Section B of Form 4684, on line 27, and enter â€œSee attached statementâ€ above line 27. Attach a statement to your tax return showing how you calculated the deductible loss (you can use the worksheet as your attachment).</span></td>
