culator: it compares the home with similar listings nearby."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average Airbnb occupancy rate in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Listings in Surfside Beach were booked on 37% of available nights over the past year. That compares with 39% for the South Carolina average. July is usually the busiest month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an Airbnb cost per night in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average booked night in Surfside Beach cost $419 before fees. Half of listings charge between $210 and $530, so bedroom count and location move the price more than the average suggests."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a permit for an Airbnb in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"None of the active Surfside Beach listings display a registration, permit or license number. That doesn't mean no rules apply, so confirm registration, permit and occupancy-tax rules with the city or county before buying."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Airbnb profitable in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, when it's run well. The average Surfside Beach Airbnb grossed $42,902 in the 12 months to September 2026, 14% above the South Carolina average of $37,525. Run by its owner, with the cleaning fee covering the cleaner and everyday costs for Airbnb's fee, utilities, supplies, upkeep and insurance, $26,382 a year (about $2,200 a month) is left before the mortgage or rent. A home that costs less than that to own or rent makes a profit, and a listing at the top-quarter mark leaves about $4,330 a month. Check a specific home in the Airbnb calculator."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When is Airbnb peak season in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"July usually pays best, averaging $11,600 per active listing over the past two years, and January usually pays least. The month-by-month table above shows how the latest 12 months played out."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Airbnb RevPAR in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each night a Surfside Beach listing was open to book earned $174 on average over the past year, booked or not. That figure, revenue per available night (RevPAR), folds price and occupancy into one number; the top 10% of listings made $389 or more."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far in advance do guests book Airbnbs in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Surfside Beach stays were booked 73 days (about two and a half months) before arrival on average over the past year, so a listing that opens its calendar late misses many bookings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long do guests stay at Airbnbs in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average Surfside Beach Airbnb stay lasted 5.2 nights over the past year. A listing took 17 reservations over the year on average."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are Airbnbs in Surfside Beach rated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Guests rate Surfside Beach Airbnbs 4.82 out of 5 on average. Guests score location highest and cleanliness lowest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the best neighborhoods for Airbnb in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Ocean Boulevard, Dogwood Drive and Garden City draw the most short-term rental interest in Surfside Beach. The neighborhood guide explains what brings guests to each."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many Airbnbs are there in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AirROI counted 551 active Airbnb listings in Surfside Beach as of September 2026. The closest tracked market is Garden City Beach, 4 km away."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are Airbnb cleaning fees in Surfside Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Surfside Beach, more than nine in ten listings add a cleaning fee. The median fee is $265, and