+<span class="heading centered smallCaps">References in Text</span>
+<p>The <a href="/topn/national_flood_insurance_act_of_1968">National Flood Insurance Act of 1968</a>, referred to in subsecs. (a), (b), (d)(1), and (e)(1), and the Act, referred to in subsec. (b), is title XIII of <a href="/rio/citation/Pub._L._90-448">Pub. L. 90â€“448</a>, <span class="date" date="1968-08-01">Aug. 1, 1968</span>, <a href="/rio/citation/82_Stat._572">82 Stat. 572</a>, which is classified principally to this chapter (Â§â€¯4001 et seq.). For complete classification of this Act to the Code, see Short Title note set out under <a href="/uscode/text/42/4001">section 4001 of this title</a> and Tables.</p>
+<p>The Federal Financial Institutions Examination Council Act of 1974, referred to in subsec. (b)(1), probably means the <a href="/topn/federal_financial_institutions_examination_council_act_of_1978">Federal Financial Institutions Examination Council Act of 1978</a>, <a href="/rio/citation/Pub._L._95-630">Pub. L. 95â€“630, title X</a>, <span class="date" date="1978-11-10">Nov. 10, 1978</span>, <a href="/rio/citation/92_Stat._3694">92 Stat. 3694</a>, which is classified principally to chapter 34 (Â§â€¯3301 et seq.) of Title 12, Banks and Banking. For complete classification of this Act to the Code, see Short Title note set out under <a href="/uscode/text/12/3301">section 3301 of Title 12</a> and Tables.</p>
+<p><a href="/rio/citation/Pub._L._103-325">Section 522(a) of Public Law 103â€“325</a>, referred to in subsec. (b)(4)(C), was in original â€œsection 522(a) of such Actâ€, which generally amended subsec. (b) of this section.</p>
+<p>This title, referred to in subsec. (e)(5)(B), (C), means title I of <a href="/rio/citation/Pub._L._93-234">Pub. L. 93â€“234</a>, <span class="date" date="1973-12-31">Dec. 31, 1973</span>, <a href="/rio/citation/87_Stat._977">87 Stat. 977</a>, which enacted this section and <a href="/uscode/text/42/4104">section 4104 of this title</a> and amended sections 4001, 4013 to 4016, 4026, 4054, 4056, and 4121 of this title.</p>
+</div>
